INT. SKATELAND ROLLER RINK - PARTY ROOM - DAY

Plastic tablecloths. A sheet cake shaped like a sneaker. Disco light spins across the wall.

ODALYS, 70s, church dress, guards the cake. PAULO REYES, 40s, a dad with a phone in each hand. KIKI, 8, birthday crown crooked. DANTE FERREIRA, 15, hood up, bored. MARISOL, 38, Paulo's sister, tying balloons. TIO BETO, 60s, mustache, holds a camcorder.

TIO BETO
Everybody in the picture! Closer!

They bunch up. Kiki leans toward the candles.

KIKI
Wait. Where's Mom?

Paulo's smile freezes.

PAULO
She's coming, mija.

DANTE
(muttering)
She said that last year.

Paulo whips around.

PAULO
Dante.

Odalys slaps the table. The cake jumps.

ODALYS
Not today. Everyone sit. Now.

Nobody sits. Marisol lets go of a balloon; it drifts to the ceiling.

MARISOL
(to Paulo)
Did you even call her?

PAULO
Three times.

KIKI
Is she not coming?

Silence. The disco light turns. Dante pulls his hood down.

DANTE
(to Kiki)
She's coming. I texted her where we are.

Paulo stares at him.

Dante's phone buzzes. He reads it, turns the screen toward Paulo. Paulo reads it and his shoulders drop.

PAULO
(to Kiki)
She's in the parking lot. Parking.

KIKI
Mom's parking!

She is already running for the door. Paulo exhales. Odalys crosses herself and lights the candles.

TIO BETO
(to himself)
Rolling. Finally rolling.

ODALYS
(to everyone)
Sing. Loud.
